  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Institutional Capacity to Address Mobility Dimensions of Crises</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Leveraging the progress made and lessons learned through the previous multi-phased global capacity strengthening programme supported by United States Department of State Bureau of Population, Refugees and Migration, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is contributing towards the Organization&#x2019;s Strategic Plan (2024-2028) objectives of saving lives and protecting people on the move while driving solutions to displacement with a focus on addressing the impacts of climate change on migration and displacement. This project is filling critical gaps in the Organization&#x2019;s capacity through bolstering operational readiness and prevention; enhancing IOM&#x2019;s distinctive response with a view of solutions to displacement; and influencing change in the humanitarian, peace and development landscape.</narrative>
  </description>
